FUN_0000_14da: zero-fill of the allocated scratch buffer — ES base restore (dynamic segment).

After the 182a/184b/0a31 allocation succeeds (struct at DGROUP:0x4f0; struct[0] now holds the real
allocated segment), 14da zeroes the buffer:  mov es,[0x4f0]; xor di,di; mov cx,(size-8)/2;
rep stosw ax=0 ; mov cx,4; rep stosw ax=0xffff  (asm 0x14ef..0x1506). Ghidra dropped the ES segment
base (rendered di as a bare host pointer starting at 0), so the very first store hit host address 0 ->
SIGSEGV. Latent until patch 025/026 made the allocator return a real segment into struct[0]. Fix: base
every store at g_mem+(es<<4)+di with es = struct[0] = DAT_1000_c4f0. Asm-verified base-0 0x14ef..0x1506.
